      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 6-membered P-heterocycle has been fused with a polyaromatic framework through intramolecular transformation of anthracene-based phosphine induced by CuCl2. The resulting water soluble phosphonium fluorophores exhibit extremely high quantum efficiency along with prominent stability and low toxicity that make them suitable for one- and two-photon imaging purposes."},
